-.BI "show " ID " " DIR/PASS
-Decrypt and print a secret.
+.BI "show [\-\-raw|\-\-render] " ID " " DIR/PASS
+Decrypt and show a secret. On a terminal the entry is rendered with
+.BR glow (1);
+when stdout is a pipe, a script or an extension it prints the raw md1 document.
+.B \-\-raw
+always prints it raw,
+.B \-\-render
+always renders (e.g. into
+.BR "less \-R" ).
+What glow receives is not the md1 document but a display\-only one: the password,
+the OTP and the field values go in code blocks or code spans, always fenced by more
+backticks than the longest run in the text itself, and field names are escaped, so
+markdown never alters what is shown (\fBa*b*c_d_\fR would otherwise render in italics).
+Only the notes are real markdown, and
+.B http(s)://
+values become links. The text goes to glow on stdin, never as an argument, and
+nothing is written to disk. If glow is missing or fails, a warning is printed and
+the raw text is shown. An entry in the old format or with an invalid structure is
+always shown raw. To copy a password use
+.BR clip :
+glow draws margins and padding around the text.
 .TP
